WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Think about this: An old county list shows
$35,000 but a

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.360
transfer is recorded. What is the current
county balance?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.260
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.480
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 10: Locate the
current custodian.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.520
A source may describe a sale, an initial
deposit, or an older holding

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.300
account. None automatically identifies
where money is held today.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.820
A file can involve a clerk, trustee,
treasurer, court registry, or state

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.380
agency. Identify the actual custodian and
distinguish its accounting role

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.720
from the role of a court deciding
entitlement.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.240
For an authorized case, request or review
the relevant official status

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.740
through the applicable process.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.460
Record the response date, source document,
balance definition, and whether

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.520
any transfer or distribution occurred.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.440
If funds moved, keep both the old and new
references.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.220
Do not turn a historical balance into a
current one simply because a webpage

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.080
still displays it. Use three separate
fields: original reported deposit,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.500
current confirmed balance, and
verification date.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.560
Leave missing values unknown.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.020
A written current response can still
contain conditions or pending matters

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.820
that must be preserved in your summary.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.020
Pause and try this.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.920
Trace a fictional county-to-state
transfer.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.460
Identify which old figure cannot be
labeled a current county balance.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.380
Quick knowledge check. An old county list
shows thirty-five thousand dollars

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.880
but a transfer is recorded.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.060
What is the current county balance?

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.360
The answer: Unknown until current custody
and accounting are verified.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.220
A transfer changes the verification task;
do not invent either a current

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.640
balance or a zero.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.980
Keep the source, the date, and the
unknowns visible.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.780
I'll see you in the next lesson.
